Commercial S3.2 fresh-prestart loopback diagnosis
=================================================

Observed at: 2026-08-29T15:56:12Z
Action: transient network-contained fresh-prestart

Safe symptom
------------

The startup probe had already completed phases 01 through 17, but the separate
fresh-prestart exited with status 2. The main service remained inactive,
Restart remained no, NRestarts remained zero, and the diagnostic contract plus
runtime authorization were restored exactly.

Proven root cause
-----------------

The bound PostgreSQL DSN uses a loopback host. The first fresh-prestart sandbox
allowed AF_UNIX only, so its database connection could not reach the local
loopback PostgreSQL listener. A credential-safe classification reported only
POSTGRES_HOST_CLASS=LOOPBACK; no host, port, database name, user or password was
written to evidence.

Correction boundary
-------------------

The transient prestart may use AF_UNIX, AF_INET and AF_INET6, but systemd
applies IPAddressDeny=any and IPAddressAllow=localhost. It receives no Telegram
token. Therefore only the local PostgreSQL loopback connection is possible;
Telegram and every external provider remain unreachable.

The wrapper also emits the prestart entrypoint's safe JSON output on failure
before returning its own fail-closed code. The prestart entrypoint never emits
exception messages or credential material.

Rollback
--------

Restore Control commit d5c100c931d17b690d5ab1932ed39068939a1f11.
This restores AF_UNIX-only prestart behavior and the proven local database
connection failure without changing application code, database or state.
